WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.601
- Hey, guys, Frito-Lay and
I have always wanted to

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.667
do something together.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:06.200
I'm a big fan of their products.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.801
In fact, I have so many snacks
and chips at my house

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.868
that if anyone needs any,
just ask me.

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:15.167
Yeah. The kids love them.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.801
Franny loves the --
I got to get it right.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:20.601
Franny loves the blue ones.
Winnie loves the red ones.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:21.634
That's what they call them,
yeah.

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:23.968
But, anyways,
so they asked me --

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.300
they had a holiday spot idea
this year,

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.267
a giant thing, and I read it,
I saw it. I loved it.

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.934
I said, "Yeah,
I'd like to do this."

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.767
And it's directed by
Dave Meyers, who is awesome.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.267
I've worked with him.
Known him for a while.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:37.667
I got to sing on it.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:41.467
So I want to thank Joel Simon at
J.S.M. MUSIC for the production.

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.167
It really worked. Poor --

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:45.133
Yeah, I mean, we did
a three-hour session

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:47.634
just to get one line out.

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:51.000
But it was -- [stammers]
you'll see it.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.200
It's like a movie, basically.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.534
It was so much fun.

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:58.801
I got to act with the CGI
Double-Dipping Monster,

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:01.367
which was really just a guy
in a green suit.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.734
And I was on wires at one point.

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.901
-Whoa.
-Because I go down the banister,

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:07.634
and they were like,
"Hey, can you slide down

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.100
the banister."
I go, "Yeah."

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.334
But when you really slide down
a banister, it's fast, so...

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:16.534
You can't get one word out.
You're like, "It's the --"

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:18.834
and that's it.
It's like, you got to go down.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:21.767
So I go,
"I can't control gravity."

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:24.067
But I got to play ten different
characters.

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:26.133
It's big. It's fun.
There's singing, dancing.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:28.734
My wife and kids are in it, too,
at the end.

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:31.701
Yeah, and I just want to thank
everyone at Frito-Lay

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:34.100
who helped make it happen.
It was honestly, top to bottom,

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.567
one of the best experiences
I've ever had.

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:40.934
I loved it.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.667
But I also wanted to mention
something cool

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:46.000
that Frito-Lay is doing
for the holidays.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.501
Together, Frito-Lay and Pepsi-Co
are going to donate

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:52.234
a total of $1 million
to Toys for Tots,

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:55.434
helping even more families enjoy
the holidays.

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.133
♪♪

00:01:57.133 --> 00:02:00.234
They're all about the spirit of
giving and sharing joy,

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:01.801
and this season you can find
specially-marked

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:04.033
holiday packages of Frito-Lay
products

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.634
that will benefit Toys for Tots
with each purchase

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:09.701
now through December 31st.
Can you see that thing?

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:12.167
Yeah, see that right there?
Yeah, here's the bag.

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:13.501
This is what I'm into now.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.968
-Steve: Cheetos.
-These are my jam.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.267
Cheetos -- I'm a Dorito --
&gt;&gt; Steve:

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:20.968
-Right.
-Any kind of Dorito.

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:23.434
-Cool Ranch.
-Smart Food.

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:25.100
Yeah. Ruffles.
-Yeah.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.300
-Lays.
-Sure.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.200
-Whatever it is.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.868
-But, no, right now.
-Cheetos.

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:31.567
-These are like magic to me.

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:32.868
-So you eat one,
it's like magic.

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:35.267
-Well, I think
it's perfectly done.

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:38.968
It's perfectly dusted with
Cheetos dust.

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:40.801
-Just with cheese.
-Yes, it's perfectly --

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:43.968
-Did you meet Chester Cheeto
during the commercial?

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:45.200
-I got to meet him.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.367
-Are you serious?
-Yeah.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:51.634
-What is he like?
-He's cheesy. Ah.

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:55.100
But anyways, I want to thank
Frito-Lay for doing this

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.701
with Toys for Tots,
and for also giving everyone

00:02:57.701 --> 00:03:00.567
in our audience their own bags
of Frito-Lay.

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:04.100
Can you -- You got them?
Let me see them.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.100
Let me see 'em right there
so we can get a good shot at it.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.267
Give 'em a good shake
right there.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:10.067
It's a shared experience.

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:11.567
Whoa!

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:12.834
Happy holidays, everybody.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:15.934
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show"!

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:24.801
♪♪

